### 7.18 Why tiny `collect()` calls are acceptable in tests

The test fixture contains only a handful of rows.

Collecting those rows makes exact assertions straightforward.

That does not justify collecting an unbounded production dataset. For large outputs, use distributed checks, bounded samples, or aggregate assertions.

Also remember that DataFrame row order is not guaranteed unless explicitly ordered. The test compares a set because order is not part of the snapshot contract.

